t assay to measure DNA methylation</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><year>2000</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>E32</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10734209</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lo</surname><given-names>YM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wong</surname><given-names>IH</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Tein</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Ng</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Hjelm</surname><given-names>NM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quantitative analysis of aberrant p16 methylation using real-time quantitative methylation-specific polymerase chain reaction</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1999</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>3899</fpage><lpage>3903</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10463578</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>21</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eads</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Danenberg</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></name><name><surname>Kawakami</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Saltz</surname><given-names>LB</given-names></name><name><surname>Danenberg</surname><given-names>PV</given-names></name><name><surname>Laird</surname><given-names>PW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>CpG island hypermethylation in human colorectal tumors is not associated with DNA methyltransferase overexpression</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1999</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>2302</fpage><lpage>2306</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10344733</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>22</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person